        "original_id": "112af738-c050-5623-a4fa-825f49dc4bbc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: King Conchobar, Cúchulainn, Queen Medb\n- Places: Ulster, Connacht, Cuailgne, Ireland, Lowland Scotland\n- Concepts: Táin, Scots language, Ulster Scots, Aikenhead surname\n\nFacts:\n- The Táin tells of the exploits of King Conchobar and his chief warrior Cúchulainn, who is called \"The Hound of Ulster.\"\n- The Táin tells of Queen Medb of Connacht invading Ulster to capture the Brown Bull of Cuailgne.\n- Ulster is a province in the north of the island of Ireland.\n- Scots is a Germanic language variety spoken in Lowland Scotland and in parts of Ulster, where the local dialect is called Ulster Scots.\n- Aikenhead is a Scots language surname of medieval Scottish origin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
